Origin: EmberBSD, AI-assisted. Local patch; not submitted upstream.

Add send-events configuration and the libudev view to wscons devices.

A consumer disables a pointer with LIBINPUT_CONFIG_SEND_EVENTS_DISABLED.
The disabled device drains its queue, reports nothing and releases the
buttons that were held down. Keyboards keep no send-events configuration.
libinput_device_get_udev_device() returns the libudev-bsd device for the
node, so consumers read ID_INPUT_* properties as they do on Linux. Path
contexts share the udev context layout.

